 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nSection iterator returns incorrect count of inner content elements\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen iterating over section inner content, the iterator is returning one extra element than expected. This affects the `iter_inner_content()` method which should return the exact number of block elements within a section.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\n\n# Load a document with multiple sections containing paragraphs and tables\ndocument = Document('sct-inner-content.docx')\n\n# Check the first section - should contain 3 elements (P1, Table T2, P3)\ninner_content = list(document.sections[0].iter_inner_content())\nprint(f\"Expected: 3 elements, Got: {len(inner_content)} elements\")\n\n# The iterator is returning 4 elements instead of the expected 3\n# This happens for all sections in the document\n```\n\nThe issue occurs when calling `iter_inner_content()` on any section - it consistently returns one more element than the actual content present in the section. For a section that should contain 3 block elements (paragraphs and tables), the iterator returns 4 elements.\n</issue>\n",
